Subject: [Boxedwine Wine 11.0] Retire idle COM surrogates using DLL lifetime

Drop dllhost's permanent reference to the hosted factory and use the server's
DllCanUnloadNow contract, keeping the module mapped while polling. Revoke the
wrapper before the final check so active factory/object/lock references keep
the server alive. Unknown or redirected server modules remain conservative.

Preserve REGCLS_SURROGATE registrations for subsequent clients, release the
reference acquired when marshalling a factory into a hosting apartment, and
retry activation if an idle server revoked its registration during lookup.

This fixes the Futuremark SystemInfo helper left running after 3DMark03 exits.
It does not classify dllhost as a Wine system process and does not implement
the complete CoRegisterSurrogate API (including multiple-DLL hosting).

Regression check when changing this patch: launch 3DMark03 with Futuremark
SystemInfo enabled, then close it using the application's own close button.
The dllhost helper and Boxedwine must exit normally. No benchmark run is needed;
do not use -nosysteminfo or close the outer Boxedwine window for this check.

Base: Wine 11.0, db11d0fe6a169c457e23d007e20404643d067aa8
Validation and limitations: docs/3dmark03-shutdown.md
Regression probe: tools/buildWine/probes/surrogate-lifetime.c

